# Database connection conventions

One client: `lib/db/env.ts` + `index.ts`. Callers use `runQuery`. Do not add a second Drizzle/Turso/Prisma path.

- `schema.ts` is a barrel. Domain tables belong in modules it re-exports.
- Column types must generate SQLite now and PostgreSQL later. No UI-presentation columns.
- DDL: `pnpm db:generate` → `lib/db/migrations/` (never hand-edit). Data: `lib/db/sql/<dialect>/*.sql`.
- Workflow and field ownership: [campaign-domain-modeling](../skills/campaign-domain-modeling/SKILL.md) ([persistence.md](../skills/campaign-domain-modeling/references/persistence.md)).

```ts
// BAD — new client, sync SQLite-only API, presentation column
import Database from "better-sqlite3";
export const db = drizzle(new Database("app.db"));
export const campaigns = sqliteTable("campaigns", {
  readinessPct: integer("readiness_pct"),
});

// GOOD — existing barrel + portable fields + async helper
import { runQuery } from "@/lib/db";
import { campaigns } from "@/lib/db/schema";
await runQuery((db) => db.select().from(campaigns));
```
